  "question": {
    "text": "Five charges $+q,+5 q,-2 q,+3 q$ and $-4 q$ are situated as shown in the figure, The electric flux due to this configuration through the surface S is :\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/ESYs0oOGMfXxPjYnJuRC4u6SJM0fVI_GIDixGUNPM6w.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "DkKzq",
      "text": "$\\frac{5 q}{\\epsilon_0}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "tLPzW",
      "text": "$\\frac{4 q}{\\epsilon_0}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "DvV7R",
      "text": "$\\frac{3 q}{\\epsilon_0}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "N2kXa",
      "text": "$\\frac{q}{\\epsilon_0}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Using Gauss's law, $\\phi=\\frac{q}{\\epsilon_0}$\nHere, $\\mathrm{q}=$ charge inside the closed surface\n$\\therefore \\phi=\\frac{q+(-2 q)+5 q}{\\epsilon_0}$\n$\\Rightarrow \\phi=\\frac{4 q}{\\epsilon_0}$",
    "image": null
  },
